      "summary": "Magento Sample Product Data - QA Validation",
      "description": "As a\n QA Analyst,\nI want\n to validate that the Magento sample product data has been correctly imported into the lower SFCC environments,\nso that\n the team can confirm the data is accurate and sufficient before it is used for development and testing activities.\nTasks\nVerify that sample products are visible and accessible in the SFCC Business Manager lower environment\nConfirm at least one product per top-level category has been imported\nValidate that products with multiple colours and sizes correctly reflect the master → variation group → variant hierarchy\nCheck that a mix of in-stock and out-of-stock variants are present and displaying the correct stock status\nLog any data discrepancies or missing products as defects\nAcceptance Criteria\nGiven the imported sample data, when reviewed in Business Manager, then all expected top-level categories contain at least one product\nGiven products with colour and size variants, when reviewed, then the master → variation group → variant hierarchy is correctly structured in SFCC\nGiven the stock status of variants, when reviewed, then both in-stock and out-of-stock variants are present and correctly flagged\nGiven any data issues found, when logged, then defects are raised and communicated to the developer for correction\nDependencies\nMagento sample product data must be imported into the lower environment before this task begins\nNotes\nMagento is the interim data source — AP21 is not currently accessible. Sample data will be replaced by the live MuleSoft/AP21 feed once the integration is available.",
